{"name":"Texas Longhorn","hex":"#e08d3c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"texas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The topmost cabin deck on a steamboat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/texas"},{"term":"longhorn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of beef cattle, having long horns, bred in Texas and other parts of southwest United States.","Ellipsis of longhorn beetle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/longhorn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Texas Longhorn","blocks":[{"text":"The Texas Longhorn is an American breed of beef cattle, characterized by its long horns, which can span more than 8 ft (2.4 m) from tip to tip. It derives from cattle brought from the Iberian Peninsula to the Americas by Spanish conquistadors from the time of the Second Voyage of Christopher Columbus until about 1512. For hundreds of years the cattle lived a semi-feral existence on the rangelands; they have a higher tolerance of heat and drought than most European breeds. The coat can be of any color or mix of colors; in some 40% of the cattle it is some shade of red, often a light red."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Texas_Longhorn_cow.jpg/330px-Texas_Longhorn_cow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_Longhorn"},{"title":"Texas","blocks":[{"text":"Texas is a state in the United States. Located in the south-central part of the country, it borders Louisiana, Arkansas, Oklahoma, and New Mexico. It also borders Mexico along the Rio Grande, and has a coastline on the Gulf of Mexico. Covering 268,596 square miles (695,660 km2) and with an estimated population of over 31.7 million residents in 2025, it is the second-largest state by both area and population. Texas is nicknamed the \"Lone Star State\" for the single star depicted on the Republic of Texas flag in 1836 during the Texas war for independence from Mexico, symbolizing Texans' enduring independent spirit and distinct national identity. The lone star design was originally flown in 1819 during the Long Expedition, an early attempt to liberate Texas from Spanish imperial rule."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Flag_of_Texas.svg/330px-Flag_of_Texas.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg/500px-Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg/1280px-Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg/500px-Texas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A steer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATexas_Longhorn_Steer_Rocksprings.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Texas_Longhorn_in_Alvin%2C_Texas.jpg/500px-Texas_Longhorn_in_Alvin%2C_Texas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Texas_Longhorn_in_Alvin%2C_Texas.jpg/1280px-Texas_Longhorn_in_Alvin%2C_Texas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Texas_Longhorn_in_Alvin%2C_Texas.jpg/500px-Texas_Longhorn_in_Alvin%2C_Texas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Texas Longhorn in Alvin, Texas","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATexas_Longhorn_in_Alvin%2C_Texas.jpg"},{"sr